// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6564 New rules for AI coding agent CLI abuse (Claude Code, Codex CLI)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6564
// Pull request author: yug3009p
// Change: new rule
// Title: AI Coding Agent CLI Execution With Permission or Sandbox Bypass
// Sigma ID: 9eb7d82c-a991-4ac4-9d76-9d6a7d9fa2b3
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Yug Patel
// Date: 2026-11-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685, execution, T1059
// Description: Detects Claude Code or the OpenAI Codex CLI being started with an option that disables approval
//   prompts or the sandbox, which lets the agent run any command without a human confirming it. The
//   s1ngularity supply chain attack (malicious Nx packages, August 2025) launched locally installed
//   AI coding agents with such options from an npm install script and asked them to search the host
//   for secrets. These options are also used legitimately to run agents unattended inside containers
//   or disposable VMs.
// False positives:
//   - Developers or CI jobs running an agent unattended inside a container or disposable VM, which is what these options are intended for
// References:
//   - https://github.com/nrwl/nx/security/advisories/GHSA-cxm3-wv7p-598c
//   - https://www.wiz.io/blog/s1ngularity-supply-chain-attack
//   - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference
//   - https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/reference
//   - https://github.com/yug3009p/agent-attack-samples
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e5a36558875aad6521daf9b6b582960eab46629f/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ai_agent_cli_permission_bypass.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\claude.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\codex.exe") and ((ProcessCommandLine contains "--dangerously-skip-permissions" or ProcessCommandLine contains "bypassPermissions" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox" or ProcessCommandLine contains "danger-full-access") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "approval_policy" and ProcessCommandLine contains "never"))
